[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Danish Gambit"]
[Variation "Danish Gambit Declined: Sorensen Defense"]
[ECO "C21"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap"]
[Themes "isolated-pawn,piece-activity"]
[Kind "main"]

1. e4 e5 2. d4 exd4 3. c3 d5 { Black hits e4 and gives back the extra pawn, which is Black's best way to meet the gambit. }
4. exd5 { Takes the pawn and opens the e-file. White is a pawn up for a moment but Black can win it back. } 4... Qxd5
5. cxd4 { Takes the pawn back and White now has a centre pawn on d4. The queen on d5 can be hit by a knight on c3 later. } 5... Nc6
6. Nf3 { Develops and defends d4 once more. } 6... Bb4+
7. Nc3 { Blocks the check with a developing move, and the knight attacks the queen. } 7... Bg4
8. Be2 { Develops and prepares castling. It also gets out of the way of the pin on f3. } 8... Bxf3
9. Bxf3 { Takes back with the bishop, which now eyes the black queen and knight. } 9... Qc4 (9... Qxd4 10. Bxc6+ bxc6 11. Qxd4)
10. Bxc6+ { Gives up the bishop pair, but ruins Black's pawns and wins time. } 10... bxc6 11. Qe2+ { Check on the e-file. } 11... Qxe2+ 12. Kxe2 { Plan: keep the king safe, put the rooks in the centre and use the pawn on d4. } *
